# Mandatory implementation behavior

- Do not use arbitrary measure, metric, KPI, chart, proof, or model-count gates.
- Do not hardcode industry-specific entities, tables, fields, formulas, pages, or models.
- Use dbt manifest unique_id as the canonical resource identifier when available.
- Do not infer PASS from arbitrary text. Read explicit status fields.
- Do not trust recorded PASS when evidence can be calculated independently.
- SQL execution and business approval are separate statuses.
- Every approved rendered KPI must map to a contract, catalog entry, query, proof, page, and visible report element.
- Missing evidence must be BLOCKED or DEFERRED, never fabricated.
- Do not weaken validators or tests to obtain a pass.
- Do not mark a task complete until the specified commands return exit code 0.
- When blocked, report the exact blocker, file, command, and required action.
- Examples are illustrative only and must never become executable requirements.